  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The investigation into the alleged illegal wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto has gained momentum, involving both political and law enforcement authorities. The National Police are set to discuss the matter during a working meeting with the legislative Commission III scheduled for November 12. Public and political reactions have been significant, with the Gerindra party urging a broader investigation to uncover those responsible. Former Chairman of the Constitutional Court Jimly Asshiddiqie has publicly supported the police efforts, suggesting the activities could constitute treason. Meanwhile, the Golkar Party has defended its chairman, Bahlil Lahadalia, against accusations connecting him to the case, with Bahlil issuing a demand for clarification or legal action. The Ministry of Human Rights has also issued public remarks regarding the severity of the act, while the police are currently coordinating with the LPSK to provide protection for six witnesses involved in the ongoing probe.",
